From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] xaudio2: Calls on a destroyed voice do nothing.

A game goes on calling a voice after DestroyVoice, which does no harm on Windows: GetState, SubmitSourceBuffer, Start, Stop,
the getters and a second DestroyVoice are all harmless there. Here the voice kept its pointer to the FAudio voice that
DestroyVoiceSafeEXT had freed, so the next call read freed memory (a mixer thread crashed in FAudioSourceVoice_GetState on a
voice the game had destroyed), and the voice's object went to the next voice created, so a late SubmitSourceBuffer queued its
buffer there.

A destroyed voice now has no FAudio voice (voice_is_gone), and each method of the source, submix and mastering voices answers
with nothing when its voice is gone: RETURN_IF_GONE and its variants stand first in the method, getters answer with zeros, and
a second DestroyVoice is ignored. The sends of a new voice leave out a destroyed voice (forget_gone_sends). The destroyed
voice's object is not handed to a new voice for LATE_CALL_GRACE_MS (10 s), counted from the destroy by GetTickCount64
(slot_is_free): a late call comes within moments of the destroy, and the object, still dead, takes it without changing a
newcomer.

The problem was found by reading bornaradusin/PC5's description of the crash (LGPL-2.1-or-later; patch 0007 of its
patches/prospero-win); the design and the code are this project's own (NOTICE.md, "PC5").
